WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Verify the review. Keep the evidence.
One real defect. One false concern. One question the code cannot answer.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Two agents inspect the same claims.
Each reply keeps the claim IDs and cites evidence. Both slots use OpenCode.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The batch count breaks its contract.
Five items at capacity two contain two full batches. The implementation returns three.

4
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:44.000
This comment does not justify a fix.
The code uses sorted(), which creates a new list. The caller’s list stays unchanged.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:56.000
An unknown requirement stays unknown.
Lexical order is observable. Whether production needs natural order is not supplied.

6
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Revisit L3. Keep the missing evidence visible.
The follow-up preserves the finding IDs and uses its two-turn default.

7
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
A review trail you can act on.
Inspect the defect. Retract the unsupported concern. Obtain the missing requirement.
